# arch-replay-mutation.cases — the case inputs both halves read, one CASE record per line.
#
# CASE|<case-id>|<request>|<rows-before>|<reader-cursor>
#
# The trace this corpus replays is not recorded rows but a request the implementation must judge. Each
# case seeds a store holding two rows (a task and its claim) and then offers one run-orchestrator
# lease request against it: `valid` is the request admission accepts, `unknown_field` is the same
# request carrying one field the request shape does not admit, and `expired_session` is the same
# request whose session expired before the event clock. rows-before is the ledger row count the
# request is offered against; reader-cursor is a consumer that has read through seq 1.
CASE|mutation-valid|valid|2|1
CASE|mutation-unknown-field|unknown_field|2|1
CASE|mutation-expired-session|expired_session|2|1
